There’s an interesting USDA review at

https://www.fs.fed.us/eng/pubs/html/98241307/98241307.html

Two of the rangefinders they assess give high accuracy even at very small distances:  Impulse 200 and Laser Atlanta Advantage.  However, these are not cheap options.  The Bushnell Lytespeed 400 is less expensive, and works to reasonable accuracy at very short distances.

Steve

