Emiliano

I'm guessing you might be analysing camera trapping data with a truncation distance of 0.008km => 8m; is that correct?

I have a guess that the ds() function is having a hard time adding adjustment terms to the hazard rate key function.  It might be the case that your data have few points of support (not many unique distances in the data).  How many unique distances does your data contain?

I can't tell if the estimates make biological sense.  You'll need to make plots of your distance histograms as well as test the goodness of fit to get a better sense of what is happening.

