Many thanks for pointing towards that paper, Len. The first paragraph of the methods explains very clearly and concisely why my previous statements about not being able to infer density from camera trap data are wrong! Extremely good to know. From Emiliano's point of view, am I right in thinking that the number of detections during his survey, which is what I think is what his analysis so far have been based on, wouldn't be quite enough. Rather, he should have the total time during which animals were detected, broken down into 'snapshots' (with distance estimated in each snapshot)?. The total deployment time during which animals were not detected would be broken down into periods of same length, and then all periods (with and without animals) are treated as point transects.

Thanks again!

Mark

