Dear all,

My name is Irene and I am a PhD student who is planning, with my colleagues in Ecuador, a distance sampling survey of spider monkeys in a tropical forest. We aim to measure perpendicular distances to the monkeys using laser range finders, but we are unsure about which range finder model should we buy. Distances are likely to be between 10-50 m.  Does anyone have been estimating distances in similar conditions and have a preferred range finder model? All recommendations/suggestions are more than welcome.

Also, another researcher, Frazer Sinclair, asked a similar question some days ago. Would you be able to share your answers to his question (if any)?

Thank you in advance!

Best regards,

Irene

